From b3cdb369fffe1569e0fcf56b1988ef0bd6833b24 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Mar 2026 14:41:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 218/273] drm/sun4i: mixer: Describe scaler types per channel

A scaler-presence bitmask cannot distinguish the VSU10, edge-detection and
VSU8 implementations found from DE3 onward. Replace it with a per-channel
scaler-type array while retaining an explicit no-scaler value.

Keep VI YUV format exposure tied to the presence of a scaler because
subsampled formats require chroma upsampling.

Signed-off-by: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
